File Name: GloveMonitorWindow.py

Necessary Packages: PySide6.QtWidgets, PySide6.QtCore

Necessary Modules (files): SensorDataProcessor, HandKinematics, HandRenderer

Overview: This file contains the code to manage the pyside monitor window. It is accessed from SensorRead3.0, and
manages the operations in HandKinematics.py, SensorDataProcessor.py, and HandRenderer.py. It does not create any
visual objects besides the monitor window (not the live animation window), which is primarily used for debugging and
interfacing basic runtime operations by the user.

Methods: All methods are kept under the GloveMonitorWindow class

__init__: This initializes the basic monitor window and associated objects, such as the hand object, animation window and
filters (low pass)

_build_ui: appends all aspects of the basic monitor window ui to our QMainWindow object

_build_menu, _build_labels, _build_buttons, _apply_layout: basic operations for building and structuring QMainWindow
elements

_centered_label, _change_view: control live display updates, such as selecting a different aspect (i.e. 'thumb') to
view and updating live information (i.e. x_acceleration).

initDisplay: makes display visible to user. Called from SensorRead3.0

terminateDisplay: removes live display object. Called from SensorRead3.0

updateData: Pipelines raw CSV data from glove to our GloveMonitorWindow interface. Called from SensorRead3.0
Additionally, our data is put through our low_pass filtering to clean all signals.

_update_kinematics: The information from updateData is sent to our rightHand (HandKinematics) object. Operations
necessary to determine live hand orientation occur there.

_update_animation: The data stored in our rightHand object is used to update the hand animationView (HandRenderer) object.

_update_labels: This updates our displayed data in our basic monitor window.

_zero_gyros: zeros gyroscope values

_record_snapshot: capture a labeled snapshot to be stored in PositionData_Snapshots

_guess_pose: utilize your random trees classifier to determine the most likely current hand position

Usage Notes:
- When zeroing the gyroscope sensors, lay your land flat on a surface and point all fingers (INCLUDING THUMB)
straight forward, touching each other. Fingers and thumb should also be flat on the surface.
- You can change the rate that the animation updates with the ANIMATION_SAMPLE_RATE_MULTIPLIER variable
on line 64
- To utilize position identification, ensure your random trees classifier exists in the models folder